    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0121" n="11" xml:id="pg11"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/1795: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Forbes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-19T12:00:00+09:00">September 19,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 19—2:31 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>150. Peiping’s 599, September 19th, 2:30 a.m.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d9-f1"/>
                    Japanese newspapers today published extras indicating a state of war between
                    Japan and China. The Foreign Office stated to a member of the staff that the
                    facts seem to be a minor clash between Japanese South Manchurian Railway guards
                    and Chinese soldiers growing out of damage to a section of railway track just
                    north of Mukden, which the Japanese Army has since occupied. The Japanese assure
                    us they are determined upon a peaceful settlement of whatever controversy
                    arises.</p>
                <p>Under the circumstances I think it would be unwise to cancel voyage home and stay
                    here as such action might be misconstrued so I shall sail on <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Empress of Japan</hi> this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Forbes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
